task: intent-english-corpus-twins
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-05
branch: feature/intent-english-corpus-twins
worktree: ../okay-wt-entwins

why: the twin guard from intent-slavic-collision found three near-twin
  pairs in `labelled` — the English corpus the SHIPPED MODEL is fitted
  on and against which every published number is measured. A native
  reader found the same defect in my Slavic arms by eye; the guard
  found it here, in the corpus nobody had pointed it at.

    [Proposal]     "Suggestion: we meet on Monday at 9."
                || "Suggest we cancel Monday and meet Wednesday instead."
    [Request]      "Send me the agenda when you get a chance."
                || "Kindly send me the agenda."
    [Notification] "FYI the meeting room has been changed to B2."
                || "The meeting has moved to the other building."

what: rewrite the second of each pair so the corpus teaches an intent
  rather than a template; turn the guard on `labelled` from a report
  into an assertion; regenerate the shipped artifact; RE-MEASURE and
  RE-PUBLISH every number that moves — 76.7%, the per-class table, the
  register shifts, the near/far stratification, the per-language rows.

this is a re-publish lane, not a tidy-up: numbers in a doc comment, a
  module page and four changelog entries are downstream of that corpus
  and some of them will change. Any that move get corrected where they
  are quoted, and the changelog entry names them.
